Feels damn good to be writing this post.

A Huge thanks to those who wrote the spoilers and Maniac's Ascension Guide.
Also thanks to Dion Nicolaas for Dudley's dungeon. I stumbled across this
somehow, It inspired me to start playing again after a long break and also
got one of my friends hooked on the game (He wanted to know why I was
finding them so funny.)

Europa was the fifth Valkyrie in a row after playing random classes for
a long time.
The previous four fell to:
A large dog called Idefix from a bones file.
A fire ant.
An arch-Lich on the level below mine town. Polymorph trap I presume?
A cockatrice I bumped into while hallucinating.

I had a fair bit of luck early on in this game. I started out by gaining
enough levels to go fishing for excalibur, before heading
for to minetown. On the way I found a lamp that turned out to be
magic, then I found another on a bones file a couple of levels below along
with a cursed bag of holding.
The minetown altar was co-aligned, this was lucky since it was the only  
altar
I found. This got me the holy water I needed to fix up that BoH and get a  
wish
out of one of the lamps (saving the other for later.) Wearing a new set of  
GDSM
and weilding the hammer my god was kind enough to give me I went and  
picked up
a luckstone from the bottom of the mines and blessed it.

Sokoban had a second bag of holding, not what I had been hoping for but  
wasn't
a problem since it turned out an amulet I had found on the oracle level was
reflection.

The quest resulted in the loss of my pet (who had decided he wanted to be a
jaguar by this stage) when it stepped on a flame trap and then drowned. But
I left the quest levels with the artifacts, a wand of death and enough  
tinned
giant meat to max my strength as soon as I was hungry enough to eat it.

After a run back to minetown for some protection I headed to the medusa  
level
where I hoped to get a shield of reflection so I could exchange my amulet  
for
a "oLS. No luck though, so the shield joined my wish list ready for the  
castle.

Both Medusa and the castle went without a hitch. The castle armoury  
yeilded a
pair of cursed -5 speed boots which I turned into something wearable with  
help
of two magic markers I aquired somewhere along the way.

The wand of wishing was (0:1) this got me that shield I wanted, gauntlets  
of
power, 2 blessed scrolls of genocide and a tshirt. With these and the help  
of
my markers my AC reached about -35. By this stage I didn't really have  
anything
else I desperately needed so I saved my lamp and the final wand charge for
an emergency.

Those genocide scrolls removed L and ; from the game. Mind flayers and  
Master
mind flayers had already fallen to good luck with thrones.

Feeling hopeful but nervous I descended to the valley of the dead, this  
was as
far as I had made it before. Last time I got here a master Lich ruined my
armour then killed me there was no chance of that this time.
I fought through to the altar where I bought some more protection I  
decided to
spend a few more marker charges and brought my AC down to -45.

Then I took a deep breath and plunged down the stairs into an area I'd  
never
been too before. From here to getting the amulet was pretty much how you'd
expect it to run. The demons and Vlad mostly went down fairly easily when I
chased them with Mojo although I used a wand of death on orcus to make sure
I'd have plenty of charges for Rodney.

After finding the vibrating square I used one of those charges to take  
care of
Rodney for the first time and went down to the sanctum where he showed up  
again
as soon as I started a fight with the high priest.
Shortly after this fight I did something very, very stupid. I run into a  
couple
of disenchanters along the way and decided I needed to re-enchant Mojo. I
thought Mojo had been drained twice down from +7, but didn't check before
reading the scroll. I lost my favourite hammer to stupidity and put my most
promising ascension attempt at risk. Would the rest of the game have been
doable with just Excalibur? I didn't want to know, so I used those two  
wishes
I'd been saving and manged to get frost brand on the second.
I enchanted it a bit but had run out of marker charges so couldn't get it  
as
high as I'd have liked. More disenchanters brought it back down to +2 at  
some
point (I'll seriously consider genociding them in future). Other than this
and Rodney showing up repeatedly the slog up to the planes was fairly
uneventful. I had prepared a couple of cursed ?oGold detection which helped
me find the portals on earth and air, I ran round fire till a monster  
stepped
in the portal there. Water I stumbled around bubbles until I found the  
portal.
On the astral plane I found myself swamped by bugs summoned so equipped a
ring of conflict. The altar I was after ended up being the third one I  
checked.
Before finding this out I died once to pestilence. I eventually made it to  
the
altar:


You offer the Amulet of Yendor to Tyr...--More--
An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...--More--
The voice of Tyr rings out: "Congratulations, mortal!"--More--
"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of Immortality!"--More--
You ascend to the status of Demigoddess...--More--

That feels good.

